From ccc6c30f58f5c76e6f4de814ec323b360336a66f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Langley <davidl@element.io>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:26:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add a `single-threaded` feature for targets without threads
 (wasm)

With the feature on, nothing in the indexing pipeline spawns a thread:

- indexing workers run on the calling thread when the pipeline is closed,
  i.e. at commit (`join_workers`), and the pipeline is unbounded so that
  `add_document` can't block waiting for a worker;
- segment-updater tasks run inline, and merges are queued and drained
  iteratively by the outermost task rather than recursing per merge;
- single-segment no-op merges are skipped, as an inline chain of them
  would never let a commit return;
- the doc-store compressor and directory watch callbacks run inline, and
  `RamDirectory` no longer holds its lock while calling the callbacks;
- `Index::writer` falls back to one worker where `available_parallelism`
  is unsupported.

The threaded build is unchanged.
---
